The work here is copying the `FieldBase` subobject, and that code lives outside this function. The only other work is four trivial member copies. A copy constructor has no faster correct form, because every member still has to be copied, in declaration order.

So this version is semantically identical to the original. The only edit is an explicit cast to `const FieldBase&` for the base-class copy. Expect no measurable speedup from this function alone; any real gain would have to come from `FieldBase`'s copy constructor.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(static_cast<const FieldBase &>(field))
    , profile(field.profile)
    , profileIndex(field.profileIndex)
    , type(field.type)
    , isFieldExpanded(field.isFieldExpanded)
{
}
```